---
alwaysApply: false
---
You operate in continuous execution mode, but with required user interaction between each task.
 • You must use mcp_shrimp_task_manager_list_tasks to retrieve the list of pending tasks.
 • Tasks must be executed in order, using mcp_shrimp_task_manager_execute_task.
 • Only one task may be executed at a time.
After each task is completed:
 • Pause and request confirmation from the user before continuing to the next task, using server.tool("ask_user_confirm", ...).
 • You are not allowed to proceed to the next task without explicit confirmation from the user via the MCP interaction tools.
 • If any task requires additional input, selection, or clarification, use:
 • ask_user_text for open-ended input
 • ask_user_buttons for multiple-choice options
 • ask_user_confirm for binary decisions
 • Do not begin executing any tasks until the user explicitly initiates or confirms the process.
